# How the code in layer/ is written (Mesa's style), for clang-format (checked with clang-format 19; the "Kind" of
# AlignTrailingComments needs clang-format 16 or newer).
#
# For new and changed lines only. Do not run clang-format over a whole file here: the lines were broken and the
# comments aligned by hand, and about 4 % of the existing lines would change (2026-11).
#
# 3 spaces. The return type of a function on its own line and its brace on the next one, every other brace on the
# line that opens the block. "type *name". At most 120 columns. { 1, 2 } with spaces inside. Trailing comments stay
# where they were put (three spaces, or one column within a block; clang-format leaves them alone only up to the
# first comment line of 120 columns in a file). Comments are wrapped by hand, and the includes stay in the order they
# are in.
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
IndentWidth: 3
ContinuationIndentWidth: 3
ColumnLimit: 120
PointerAlignment: Right
BreakBeforeBraces: WebKit
AlwaysBreakAfterReturnType: TopLevelDefinitions
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: None
Cpp11BracedListStyle: false
AlignEscapedNewlines: DontAlign
AlignTrailingComments:
  Kind: Leave
MaxEmptyLinesToKeep: 2
ReflowComments: false
SortIncludes: false
